--
libstdc++ 13 <format>: std::format("{}", 42).  Fixed in earlier rounds: the
floating-point formatter selected for int, the visitor's `this' capture, the
primary formatter template, the per-specialization lambda closures,
formatter<const char *, char>::format, and the output of enumeration
bit-field constants (cpp11_enum_bit_field_constant_output).  Symbolic
execution did not terminate because the _Arg_store temporary of
make_format_args was destroyed before vformat read the argument through
basic_format_args (cpp98_temporary_lives_until_end_of_full_expression), and
comparisons of the _Spec bit-fields of enumeration type stayed symbolic
(cpp11_enum_bit_field_constant_comparison_simplified).  It now verifies in
about 70 s and 2.7 GB, which ran out of memory on CI's runners, hence
THOROUGH; test_format_typecheck.desc keeps the conversion in CORE.  g++ 13
accepts this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
KNOWNBUG (scaling limit): it needs 2.65 GB, above the 2.5 GB that CI's
CBMC_TEST_MEMLIMIT allows ("SAT checker ran out of memory" in the THOROUGH
job); test_format_typecheck.desc covers the type checking.
